# Web security

The always-on security rule wins if this file disagrees with it. Header policy already lives in `apps/web/src/lib/security-headers.ts` and is covered by `security-headers.test.ts`. Change that module instead of pasting a second policy.

## Content Security Policy

- Production scripts use the per-request nonce from `createScriptNonce`. Do not add `'unsafe-inline'` to `script-src` in production, and do not add a CDN origin.
- `frame-ancestors` is path-specific. Standalone stays `'none'`. `/embed/v1` uses the shared host allowlist (`WEB_EMBED_FRAME_ANCESTORS`, `WEB_PORTAL_FRAME_ANCESTORS`, `PORTAL_FRAME_ANCESTORS`). An empty allowlist stays `'none'`.
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY` applies only when `embedFramingAllowed` is false. Do not send `DENY` on an embed response that the allowlist permits to be framed.
- `frame-src` comes from `frameSrcForPath`. Do not set a global `frame-src 'none'`.
- HSTS is `max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`, and only when the request is HTTPS (`shouldSendHsts`). Do not add `preload` unless that module already does.
- Keep `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, the existing `Referrer-Policy`, and `Permissions-Policy`.

## XSS, scripts, and forms

- Do not inject unsanitized HTML or assign user HTML to `innerHTML`.
- Do not add a third-party script. Prefer the dependencies the app already ships.
- State-changing forms keep the existing CSRF and cookie session. Validate on the server. The client check is not the security boundary.
- Do not put secrets in the URL, the document, or `localStorage`.

## Embed

Wizard, Login, and change-password never mount on `/embed/v1`. Embed chrome comes only from `GET /session` `session.embed`.
